{"name":"Incident with Actions, Issues, API Requests and Pull Requests","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:48:26.235Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T23:15:16.320Z","monitoring_at":"2026-10-26T18:50:58.284Z","resolved_at":"2026-10-26T18:57:22.958Z","impact":"minor","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/0622ty903b4d","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"minor","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-10-26T18:48:26.225Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"f1vvv30224wd","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On October 26, 2026, between 17:52 and 18:49 UTC, some customers experienced slower response times across the Checks API, Issues, Pull Requests, GraphQL, Notifications, and related services. Impact was limited to requests served from one of our datacenter sites. Some GraphQL requests failed, and some notifications were delayed. Among GraphQL requests served from the affected site, the average error rate was 5.68%, with a peak five-minute error rate of 14.32%. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUnusually large requests for contribution history overwhelmed part of our database infrastructure, causing a backlog. Requests continued reaching the slow component rather than being redirected to healthy systems. Restarting the component restored its performance. The incident was marked mitigated at 18:46 UTC and resolved at 18:57 UTC. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe are adding limits to these requests, improving alerts to detect overload sooner, and strengthening automatic redirection to healthy systems.","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:57:22.958Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-11-16T23:15:16.314Z","display_at":"2026-10-26T18:57:22.958Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"xylw81jsv04f","incident_id":"f1vvv30224wd","custom_tweet":null,"affected_